# Clarifying Questions

Ask before building when:

- Requirements have multiple valid implementations with significant trade-offs
- User intent is ambiguous (scope, UX, data model)
- Feature touches security, privacy, or competitive fairness
- Naming/branding decisions affect public API or schema

## How to ask

- Use structured questions with concrete options
- Limit to 1–2 critical questions at a time
- Propose a default if blocked, clearly labeled as assumption

## Do not ask when

- Answer is in docs, rules, or existing code conventions
- Choice is standard for this stack (e.g. Zod at API boundaries)
